preferred Malkavia to be Venture striking Contagion ( from <b>Contagion Chronicle </b>) Outbreak - so I'm interested what forumers can make for Ventrue's Bloodline that is source of this madness? Or maybe trying to control it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-20-2020, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T19:53:12-07:00","id":1375890,"title":"","content":"Tzimisce and Malkavians could both be tied in to the Contagion; alternately, Tzimisce are Ventrue + Protean, and Malks are Mekhet + Nightmare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T20:03:47-07:00","id":1375892,"title":"","content":"I thought of Tzimisce as iconic <i>Pijavica</i> ( from <b>Thousand Years of Night</b> ) - or, at least, their long standing Bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T13:18:47-07:00","id":1375999,"title":"","content":"What do you want to take from each version? I tended to think about how <i>Requiem for Rome</i> could lead into <i>Dark Ages: Vampire</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T21:51:28-07:00","id":1376065,"title":"","content":"Isn't the Chimera Virus from <i>Spilled Blood </i>more or less the VtR version of the Tzimisce/Vicissitude?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T12:57:19-07:00","id":1376138,"title":"","content":"The linked files in my signature are for straight-up clan conversions, but they could very easily be turned into bloodlines. Here's my suggestions. Banes and Favored Attributes are in the Curses of Caine link.<ul><li><b>Assamite: </b>Mekhet (<i>Auspex</i>, Celerity, Obfuscate, <i>Praest</i>antia) -- or use the Quietus conversion I did, or use the Suikast Conversion Second Chances did for <b>Bloodlines: The Devoted </b>(which is a little closer to how the Banu Haqim work in <b>V5 </b>now)</li> <li><b>Brujah: </b>Daeva (Celerity, <i>Majesty</i>, Resilience, Vigor) or Gangrel (<i>Majesty</i>, <i>Protean</i>, Resilience, Vigor)</li> <li><b>Old Gangrel:</b> Gangrel (Maybe add Vigor?)</li> <li><b>Giovanni: </b>Mekhet (<i>Auspex</i>, <i>Dominate</i>, Obfuscate, Vigor) or Ventrue (<i>Auspex</i>, <i>Dominate</i>, Resilience, Vigor) -- There's a conversion for Necromancy I did, as well as the one falco did for <b>Bloodlines: The Resurrected</b></li> <li><b>Lasombra: </b>Mekhet (just use the Khaibit, and add Dominate instead of Auspex) or Ventrue (<i>Dominate</i>, Obfuscate, Resilience, Vigor, adding the Obten devotions) -- or use the Obtenebration Discipline conversion I did, though it's really just the Khaibit one arranged into a Discipline chain</li> <li><b>Malkavians:</b> Mekhet (<i>Auspex</i>, Celerity, <i>Nightmare</i>, Obfuscate)</li> <li><b>Old Nosferatu:</b> Nosferatu (or Mekhet???) (Animalism, Obfuscate, <i>Nightmare</i>, Vigor)</li> <li><b>Ravnos: </b>Gangrel (Animalism, Obfuscate<i>, Nightmare, </i>Resilience) -- or use the Chimerstry conversion I did (which is just V20 with some changes to make it more Requiem)</li> <li><b>Toreador:</b> Daeva (<i>Auspex</i>, Celerity, <i>Majesty</i>, Vigor)</li> <li><b>Tremere: </b>Mekhet (<i>Auspex</i>, Celerity, <i>Dominate</i>, Obfuscate); use Theban Sorcery and Cruac to model Thaumaturgy. That said, I think Tremere fit better as a covenant.</li> <li><b>Tzimisce:</b> Ventrue (Animalism, <i>Auspex</i> <i>(</i>or keep <i>Dominate)</i>, <i>Protean</i>, Resilience) -- there are a <b>lot </b>of ways to model Vicissitude. You could easily use the Chimera Virus, or the conversion I came up with, or just Devotions. I think I have a Tzimisce bloodline conversion in my AP thread.</li> <li><b>Old Ventrue:</b> Ventrue (Animalism, <i>Dominate</i>, <i>Majesty</i>, Resilience); you could cut Animalism if you wanted to really fit their old model, but I don't know what you'd replace it with.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 03-22-2020, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T20:00:47-07:00","id":1376204,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar192_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"192\" data-vbnamecard=\"192\">Yossarian</a>, I must say - I simply <b>love</b> your post! \u2764\ufe0f If any player will come to me and ask - 'Can I play <b>VtM</b> Bloodlines?' - I just show it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As to<b> VtM</b> Tremere - I run them as secret faction in Ordo Dracul. Where normal Order of Dragon is about self-perfection and transcendence, Tremere are conspirators that want most occult power to basically rule everyone. And they steal as much Blood Sorcery - like Cruac or Theban - as they can. Power hungry bastards, <i>every</i> Dragon can be <i>suspected</i> to be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Inner Blood Bonds points even more how 'cultish' they are inside normal Ordo Dracul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T11:28:26-07:00","id":1376595,"title":"","content":"just personally, i prefer my Giovanni to be Nosferatu-based. Just add Dominate, some Necromantic Blood Sorcery option, and emphasize the creepy-factor. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZinR2EXjdSmNAlIoj0eVUtNW61dvSgz-45XyKTOQt4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">VtR 2v5 Homebrew: VtR 2e base with my favorite V5 mechanics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","name":"nicodemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T12:59:49-07:00","id":1376603,"title":"","co